{"name":"Doodle","hex":"#fbdca8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"doodle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fool, a simpleton, a mindless person.","A small mindless sketch, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To draw or scribble aimlessly.","To engage in something non-seriously; fiddle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doodle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Doodle","blocks":[{"text":"A doodle is a drawing made while a person's attention is otherwise occupied. Doodles are simple drawings that can have concrete representational meaning or may just be composed of random and abstract lines or shapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Luise_Kritzelzeichnung.jpg/330px-Luise_Kritzelzeichnung.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doodle"},{"title":"Doodle (website)","blocks":[{"text":"Doodle is an online calendar tool for time management and coordinating meetings. It allows users to schedule and make arrangements collaboratively, among other features. Doodle is available on desktop and mobile platforms. Founded in 2007, the company is headquartered in Zürich and has offices in Berlin, Belgrade, Atlanta and New York City."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1a/Doodle_webpage_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doodle_(website)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Pushkin_doodle.jpg/500px-Pushkin_doodle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Pushkin_doodle.jpg/500px-Pushkin_doodle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A typical page from Pushkin's manuscript","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APushkin_doodle.jpg"